Actually, should bindBoard also handle disconnecting the previous RO? The issue says "on destroy and on redraw." If we store ro on state.dom, then on redraw the old state.dom.ro is orphaned (state.dom gets replaced) — so we have to explicitly disconnect the old one in redrawAll before replacing state.dom. That way bindBoard only needs to assign the new ro.

